cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Se usi Auscultrix, citalo così. / If you use Auscultrix, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Auscultrix: listening, generative soundscape and comforting media in a browser extension that computes on the device"
version: 6.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LoremYpsum-cmd/auscultrix"
url: "https://loremypsum-cmd.github.io/auscultrix/"
authors:
  - given-names: Rosario Orazio
    family-names: Caccamo
abstract: >-
  Manifest V3 browser extension (Chrome, Firefox, Safari) that reads a declared
  mood on the device and offers music, a real-time generative soundscape and
  comforting media along an ISO-principle trajectory in the valence-arousal
  plane. Includes an affect-to-sound mapping with stated sources, acoustic
  verification on the engine output (ITU-R BS.1770-4 loudness, onset
  detection, spectral centroid), external validation of the text engine on
  English and Italian human-annotated corpora, and a Pure Data twin.
  Not a medical device.
keywords:
  - generative audio
  - soundscape
  - sound design
  - Web Audio
  - Pure Data
  - ISO principle
  - circumplex model
  - affective computing
  - sentiment analysis
  - privacy by design
  - browser extension
  - Manifest V3
